# Edge Microgateway Functional Test Suite

Self-healing, deterministic E2E functional test suite for Apigee Edge Microgateway.

## Architecture (`test-functional/`)

| File | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| `NightlyTests.sh` | Declarative suite runner (`LIFECYCLE_SETUP`, `FUNCTIONAL_TESTS`, `LIFECYCLE_TEARDOWN`). |
| `testEMG.sh` | Self-contained test cases (`test*` functions following `Arrange -> Act -> Assert -> Restore`). |
| `testhelper.sh` | Test harness, mode resolution, auto OAuth2 token minting, `50ms` readiness polling, persistent Apigee Cloud fixtures (`ensureApigeeFixtures`), and DRY assertion helpers. |

---

## Running Tests (Local & CI)

Export Apigee credentials (`MOCHA_ORG` defaults to `connectors-test2`, `MOCHA_ENV` defaults to `test`):

```bash
export MOCHA_USER="emg-ciuser@google.com"
export MOCHA_PASSWORD="<password>"
```

### 1. Current Branch / Local Repo Code (`branch` mode — Default & Presubmit CI)
Runs directly against the checked-out repository (`node cli/edgemicro`) without global installation:

```bash
npm run test:functional
# or
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh
```

### 2. Packaged Repository Build (`master` mode — Continuous & Release CI)
Packs the current repository (`npm pack`) and installs it globally (`npm install -g`) to verify the packaged artifact:

```bash
npm run test:functional:master
# or
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh master
```

### 3. Public npm Registry Release (`npm` mode)
Installs and tests the published version from the public npm registry (`edgemicro@latest` or a specific version):

```bash
npm run test:functional:npm
# or
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh npm
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh npm:3.3.3
```

### 4. Run a Single Isolated Test Case
Pass any test function name as an argument to execute only that test case (along with setup/teardown):

```bash
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh testZookeeperDowntimeResilience
cd test-functional && ./NightlyTests.sh npm testQuota
```

---

## Adding a New Test Case

1. Define a self-contained `test<FeatureName>()` function in `testEMG.sh` using the built-in DRY primitives:
   - `emg_config_reload '<yaml.path>' <val> ...` — Updates config and waits (`50ms` poll) for IPC worker reload.
   - `assert_proxy_status <expected_http_code> [path] [header_name] [header_val]` — Executes request and asserts HTTP status.
   - `emg_reset_log` / `assert_log_has <pattern> [secondary]` / `assert_log_lacks <pattern>` — Asserts gateway log output.
2. Add `test<FeatureName>` to the `FUNCTIONAL_TESTS` array in `NightlyTests.sh`.
